Design decisions:
- Sink wrapping over per-emit-site passing. FR3 says every event in a
  run; there are roughly two dozen emit sites and the first one missed
  would be an invisible gap. The wrapper makes the claim structural.
- Existing metadata wins on merge: MergeMetadata(launcher, existing). A
  host part converter setting its own metadata knows something the
  launcher does not.
- eventMetadata returns nil rather than an empty Metadata when there is
  nothing to report, so the omitempty field stays absent instead of
  serializing as {}.
- nodePath reads NodeProvenanceFrom, the field aguigraph plumbs, rather
  than re-deriving provenance, per the plan's instruction not to
  duplicate that track's ownership.

GOLDEN UPDATES — three, and worth scrutiny since editing a golden to fit
the code is the failure mode this practice exists to prevent:
- agui/graph_baseline_test.go (plain-agent, from track 2)
- agui/proto_baseline_test.go (feature-free, from this track)
- agui/interrupt_baseline_test.go (tool_call wire, from track 1)

Attaching metadata to EVERY event cannot be byte-identical by
construction, so these could not survive FR3 unchanged. Before
regenerating each, the rest of the stream was proven untouched: a
temporary 'delete(ev.Raw, "metadata")' in each normalizer made all three
pass against their PREVIOUS contents, showing no reordering and no
dropped fields. Each golden now carries a comment recording what changed
and why.

Note this also breaks aguihitl_20260908 acceptance criterion 6
('tool_call resume byte-identical'). That criterion scoped a refactor
that was meant to change nothing; FR3 is a deliberate later protocol
addition. The interrupt's own metadata.adk block is untouched — only the
new event-level key differs.

